WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:17.316
stared in shock as bits and pieces of his house went flying everywhere.

2
00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:22.620
Then a huge plank flew out of the cloud of thick smoke, almost hitting him in the head.

3
00:00:27.864 --> 00:00:29.286
Zann snapped out of his stupor.

4
00:00:30.547 --> 00:00:32.028
He nudged Zing with his foot.

5
00:00:32.608 --> 00:00:36.531
The dragon was groggy but already beginning to emerge from the Flash Freeze.

6
00:00:37.232 --> 00:00:39.834
That was one especially good thing about fire whistlers.

7
00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:43.297
Even the strongest magic couldn't keep them down for long.

8
00:00:43.657 --> 00:00:44.498
They were too stubborn.

9
00:00:44.518 --> 00:00:47.180
"Wake up, boy," Zann urged the dragon.

10
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.881
"We've got to get out of here."

11
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:52.344
He doubted the stranger could have survived that explosion.

12
00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:56.748
But then Zann remembered the strong energy crackling between the man's fingers.

13
00:00:57.428 --> 00:00:58.850
He'd better not take any chances.

14
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.532
"I'll go find Darb," he murmured.

15
00:01:02.636 --> 00:01:05.518
Darb might be a Void, but he was smart and practical.

16
00:01:06.138 --> 00:01:08.079
Maybe he could help Zann figure out what to do.

17
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.740
Zann took off running.

18
00:01:10.481 --> 00:01:15.624
Zing shook off the last of the spell and flew after him, chattering irritably and breathing out small

19
00:01:15.704 --> 00:01:16.484
puffs of smoke.

20
00:01:17.165 --> 00:01:20.106
They found Darb in the same part of the swamp where Zann had left him.

21
00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.148
He looked startled when he saw Zann coming with Zing.

22
00:01:23.168 --> 00:01:26.610
"What happened to you two?"

23
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:27.371
he asked.

24
00:01:28.071 --> 00:01:29.452
Zann glanced down at himself.

25
00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:31.337
His clothes were disheveled.

26
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:34.260
Debris stuck to his sleeves, and he was covered in dust.

27
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.321
"Something crazy.

28
00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:37.182
he began.

29
00:01:37.822 --> 00:01:40.324
He told Darb the whole story as quickly as he could.

30
00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:42.786
By the end Darb looked alarmed.

31
00:01:42.806 --> 00:01:45.989
"That guy used a Flash Freeze on Zing?"

32
00:01:46.349 --> 00:01:48.211
he exclaimed, hurrying over to the dragon.

33
00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:49.772
"Come here, little buddy.

34
00:01:50.092 --> 00:01:51.233
Let's make sure you're okay."

35
00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:53.935
"He tried to use one on me too!"

36
00:01:54.496 --> 00:01:55.196
Zann exclaimed.

37
00:01:55.216 --> 00:01:58.019
"What kind of crazy person does that?"

38
00:01:58.759 --> 00:01:59.300
"I don't know."

39
00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.441
Darb looked at him.

40
00:02:00.461 --> 00:02:05.105
"Do you think Boz was still in the house when it you know exploded?"

41
00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:07.167
Zann shook his head.

42
00:02:07.187 --> 00:02:10.229
"That guy said something about taking me to Boz.

43
00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.132
I'd better try to contact my grandfather."

44
00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:20.318
Zann conjured up a message moth and quickly inscribed a simple message on its wings: Where are you?

45
00:02:20.338 --> 00:02:24.461
"Find Boz," he said, waving the message moth off.

46
00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:27.104
The message moth started to flap away.

47
00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.823
But within a few seconds, it came back, fluttering in helpless circles.

48
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:34.404
Darb frowned as he watched.

49
00:02:34.424 --> 00:02:37.186
"It can't locate him," he said softly.

50
00:02:37.206 --> 00:02:41.249
"Do you think Zann's heart flip-flopped in his chest.

51
00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.811
It had been difficult enough to deal with his parents' disappearance.

52
00:02:45.432 --> 00:02:47.934
What would he do if he lost his grandfather as well?

53
00:02:47.954 --> 00:02:52.797
"No!" Zann blurted out, not letting himself think any more about that.

54
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:54.658
"I'm sure he's okay.

55
00:02:55.038 --> 00:02:56.920
We just need to figure out where he is."

56
00:02:59.776 --> 00:03:02.217
The stranger stepped out of the ruins of Zann's house.

57
00:03:02.957 --> 00:03:07.139
He'd barely had time to throw up a strong Shield spell before the place had exploded.

58
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.700
That explosion had been an unlucky break.

59
00:03:10.361 --> 00:03:12.102
The Red boy had been especially quick.

60
00:03:13.122 --> 00:03:18.084
The energy from his emergency Zap had collided with the Flash Freeze, causing the blast.

61
00:03:20.085 --> 00:03:23.627
And now the explosion was likely to draw unwanted attention.

62
00:03:23.647 --> 00:03:26.428
"Never mind," the man muttered.

63
00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.521
"I just need to find the boy before he tells anyone about me."

64
00:03:31.142 --> 00:03:31.602
But how?

65
00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:35.063
He could return to the fortress and check the Secret Eye.

66
00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:41.486
But the Secret Eye merely showed the presence and location of Magica's Reds; it didn't show their identities.

67
00:03:42.406 --> 00:03:44.627
The boy would be one red dot among many.

68
00:03:45.347 --> 00:03:45.828
Or would he?

69
00:03:46.848 --> 00:03:51.450
Glancing down at the debris, the man happened to spot the charred remains of one of those happy

70
00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.710
family blink images.

71
00:03:53.531 --> 00:03:56.452
Grabbing it, he stared at the Red boy's grinning face.

72
00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.141
The man smiled.

73
00:03:58.401 --> 00:03:59.662
The image should do the trick.

74
00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:01.944
Yes, it should do nicely.

75
00:04:02.064 --> 00:04:07.929
"There." Zann rubbed his hands together and pointed at the cave entrance.

76
00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.771
A dark curtain instantly fell over it.

77
00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:13.734
"That will keep out anyone we don't want in here."

78
00:04:14.415 --> 00:04:15.475
He looked around the cave.

79
00:04:15.816 --> 00:04:19.779
He and his friends had gathered here many times, and no adults knew about it.

80
00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.941
It was the perfect hiding place.

81
00:04:22.621 --> 00:04:25.344
The entrance was already well hidden by thick brush.

82
00:04:26.108 --> 00:04:31.193
Zann's simple Visual Blocking spell meant nobody could see in even from a few inches away.

83
00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:36.477
Zann had used the same type of spell many times to trick Zing during their games.

84
00:04:36.497 --> 00:04:38.539
"Okay," Darb said.

85
00:04:38.559 --> 00:04:39.460
"Now what?"

86
00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.903
He was patting Zing, who still looked tired and uneasy.

87
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.505
Zann realized he was exhausted too.

88
00:04:46.226 --> 00:04:48.848
He'd used up most of his energy creating their hideout.

89
00:04:50.112 --> 00:04:54.596
First he'd had to run a quick Life Force Locator to make sure the cave was clear of

90
00:04:54.756 --> 00:04:55.857
any dangerous creatures.

91
00:04:56.918 --> 00:05:00.781
Then he'd conjured up a few lights so he could see what he was doing.

92
00:05:01.482 --> 00:05:03.123
And finally, there was the curtain.

93
00:05:03.784 --> 00:05:08.688
Being a Red gave Zann more power than most kids his age, but after all that, he'd hit

94
00:05:08.728 --> 00:05:09.189
his limit.

95
00:05:09.829 --> 00:05:11.190
He flopped down against the wall.

96
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.633
"I need to figure out where Boz went," he said.

97
00:05:14.653 --> 00:05:17.276
"That guy at my house said he knew him.

98
00:05:18.064 --> 00:05:20.265
I have no idea if he was telling the truth."

99
00:05:21.145 --> 00:05:21.926
Darb shrugged.

100
00:05:21.946 --> 00:05:24.347
"Why would someone lie about something like that?"

101
00:05:24.987 --> 00:05:25.787
Zann sighed.

102
00:05:25.807 --> 00:05:27.988
Darb was much too trusting.

103
00:05:28.688 --> 00:05:30.849
He always wanted to believe the best about people.

104
00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.250
Zann had been the same way himself once.

105
00:05:33.931 --> 00:05:36.372
But his parents' disappearance had changed that.

106
00:05:37.352 --> 00:05:38.773
"Think about it," he said.

107
00:05:39.553 --> 00:05:42.134
"Reds have been disappearing all over Magica.

108
00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:47.016
Then this weirdo shows up at my house, and suddenly Boz is missing.

109
00:05:47.816 --> 00:05:53.368
The guy has to be involved with whatever the palace was—" He stopped talking with a gasp as

110
00:05:53.408 --> 00:05:57.517
the magic curtain shattered, and a fast-moving figure burst into the cave.
